---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Link from '../components/Link';

import {
  author,
  jobTitle,
  socialLinks,
  cleanJobTitle
} from '../config/site.ts';

import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import meImage from '../assets/me.jpg';

const title = "About | " + author + " - " + jobTitle;
const description = "Learn about " + author + "’s approach to building joint ecosystems of hardware and software. Discover his principles of shared understanding, structural integrity, and architectural clarity.";
const keywords = author + ", engineering philosophy, systems architecture, hardware-software bridge, shared understanding, 0-to-1 phase, software engineering rigor, tech leadership";
const localImage = "/og/about.png";
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  keywords={keywords}
  localImage={localImage}
>
  <section class="flex-card">

    <!-- Profile Photo -->
    <div class="profile-image-floater">
        <Image
          src={meImage}
          alt="Portrait of {author}"
          width={160}
          height={160}
          loading="eager"
        />
    </div>

    <!-- Text Content -->
    <div>
      <h1>About Me</h1>

      <p>
        I am a <strong><span class="whitespace-nowrap">{cleanJobTitle}</span></strong> specializing in the intersection of hardware and software. My work is driven by a single conviction: the most impactful technology is built when we treat silicon and code as a <strong>joint ecosystem</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>The Journey to the "Bridge"</h2>

      <p>
        My fascination with systems began with a computer and no internet — a constraint that forced me to understand how software actually talks to the machine. That early curiosity evolved into a career focused on <strong>Hardware-Software Co-Design</strong>.
      </p>

      <p>
        Today, I build the core system layers — spanning <strong>compilers, simulators, and embedded firmware</strong> — that eliminate the inefficient handovers between disciplines.
        I believe that by bringing software engineering rigor to <strong>hardware-software co-design</strong>, we enable a joint ecosystem where silicon architecture and system software are developed in harmony. This ensures that the final systems are not just high-performance, but also sustainable and built on a foundation of shared clarity.
      </p>

      <h2>Where I Thrive: The "0 to 1" Phase</h2>

      <p>
        I am at my best in the <strong>design and innovation phases</strong>, where the solution space is wide open and the architecture is yet to be defined. I find deep professional fulfillment in "0 to 1" projects, where I can:
        <ul>
          <li>Establish a holistic system architecture from the start.</li>
          <li>Build the tooling and CI pipelines that enable rapid, reliable iteration.</li>
          <li>Turn abstract hardware constraints into opportunities for software elegance.</li>
        </ul>
      </p>

      <h2>Engineering with Purpose</h2>

      <p>
        At my core, I believe good engineering is about <strong>shared understanding</strong>. Technical excellence matters, but its true value is unlocked when a team moves forward with clarity and purpose.
      </p>

      <p>
        I work pragmatically, navigating real-world trade-offs without losing sight of the broader goal. Whether I am architecting an API or aligning a cross-functional team, I aim for <strong>logical clarity and reliability</strong> — ensuring the systems we build are resilient, purposeful, and easy for others to build upon.
      </p>

      <h2>Beyond the Code</h2>

      <p>
        Outside of engineering, I explore the human side of technology. I am fascinated by psychology, the dynamics of communication, and the art of explaining complex topics simply. These interests directly influence my leadership style and my approach to remote-first collaboration.
      </p>

      <p>
        I share my evolving thoughts on engineering efficiency and leadership on my <Link href="/blog">blog</Link>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="muted-top-rule">Next Steps</h2>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Technical Context:</strong> Explore my <Link href="/portfolio">project portfolio</Link></li>
        <li><strong>Professional Background:</strong> <Link href="/resume" download>Download my Résumé (PDF)</Link> or <Link href="/resume-overview">view details online</Link></li>
        <li><strong>Let's Connect:</strong> I am always open to discussing complex system architectures, RISC-V, or remote-first collaborations. Reach out via <Link href={socialLinks.email}>email</Link> or <Link href={socialLinks.linkedin}>LinkedIn</Link>.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
